Rapid Connection is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] of [[Org/Prime Meridian/index|Prime Meridian]] that helps run the trains of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]]. It is one of three great Hearts Prime Meridian installed to coordinate [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]'s transport about a century ago. It holds keystone 14, the one nearest the [[Sin and Tonic]], and collects paintings, oil or acrylic on canvas.

Its servants are wired like the rest of the Org's staff, with rods and piping of dull metal driven into their skin and their throats. One of them met the Party in a partitioned loading bay at the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]] and asked what they had to sell. They had no painting, and they were sent away.

It speaks through car radios. When the Party drove away from the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/Prime Meridian Sub Transit Nexus|Sub Transit Nexus]], their radio turned itself to a dead frequency and a voice gave them directions; they noted the frequency as 980.2 on the AM dial.

The Party came back to the nexus with a [[People/Kellum Quinn|Kellum Quinn]], *Second Meaning*, and this time a servant let them in. [[People/Hogan Voss Darkmoor|Archmechanic Darkmoor]] took them down a slow freight elevator to Rapid Connection's fane: a circular stone path over thousands of gears of the same dull metal that runs in the Org's rods, each turning or reversing on its own rather than in the steady march of a watch. Rapid Connection has no mouth; it speaks by working its gears against one another into tones that copy human speech, where they had only ever heard it through mouthpieces. Darkmoor said they were the first people outside the Org let in to see it.

The Heart knew they had a painting and first offered gold, free transit through [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], priority and access to Prime Meridian's shipping lights rather than part with its collection. They held out for the keystone, and [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] put it that they would be forever in its debt and would bring it any art they found. It agreed. [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] threw the painting into its central cortex, and a force in the Heart stripped the outer paint away: under the skyline of the Aurideon, *Second Meaning* hid the [[Pharos]], covered over. The Heart gave over keystone 14 in an ornate golden box and waived all Prime Meridian fees for the Party's travel, roads as well as rails. The stone is a cut blue gem like a plumb bob; [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] read it as a key to a sealed compartment of some kind, with something in it that only receives. Arctos asked what else it liked besides paintings, and it said trains.

The Archmechanic said the Party would be the first people outside Prime Meridian to see it since its birth more than two hundred years before.
